            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0348" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.032/103: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-08T10:00:00-05:00">November 8, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>226. Department’s 127, November 7, 6 p.m.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d218-f1"/> Decree
                    convoking legislative bodies in extraordinary session on November 10th, next,
                    has been promulgated. Legislature will assemble on the 10th and organize. When
                    organized, both bodies will report to President Roy who will then call them to
                    meet as National Assembly. It will take about a week to organize, including the
                    examination of credentials.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
